WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
Genesis gives humans a striking command.

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.720
Fill the earth, and subdue it.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.730
Have dominion over every living thing.

4
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:14.130
In 1967, the historian Lynn White blamed
one reading of that word for part of

5
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.020
the ecological crisis.

6
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.120
Today the questions are urgent: pollution,

7
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.360
global warming, and
resources that can run out.

8
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.680
So if God gave humans
dominion over the earth,

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.960
can we use it however we like?

10
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.360
In this mission, you'll
read the key verses,

11
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.500
and meet two very different
readings of dominion.

12
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.630
Then you'll see what Christians
actually do about it,

13
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.210
and test the claim that humans may use
the earth's resources as they wish.

14
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.950
Your mission: find out whether dominion
means humans can use the earth however

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.680
they like.
